schedule:
1)   Review: Basic Concepts; Energy Transfer by Heat and Work; Mechanical Forms of work; 1st Law of thermodynamics; Energy Conversion Efficiency; Phase-Change Processes of Pure Substance; Property Diagrams; Energy Balance of Closed Systems; u, h, Cp of Ideal Gases, Solids and Liquids;
2)   Mass and Energy Analysis of Control Volumes: Conservation of Mass; Flow Work and the Energy of a Flowing Fluid; Energy Analysis of Some Steady-Flow Engineering Systems; Energy Analysis of Unsteady-Flow Processes;
3)   2nd Law of thermodynamics:; Heat Engines; Reversible and Irreversible Processes; Carnot Cycle; Carnot Heat Engine;
4)   Entropy: Entropy; Isentropic Processes; Δs of Liquids, Solids and Ideal Gases; Reversible Steady-Flow Work; Minimizing the Compressor Work; Isentropic Efficiencies of Steady-Flow Devices Entropy Balance;
5)   Exergy: Exergy Change of a System; Exergy Transfer by Heat, Work, and Mass; Exergy Balance: Closed Systems; Exergy Balance: Control Volumes;
6)   Gas Power Cycles: Basic Considerations in the Analysis of Power Cycles; The Carnot Cycle; Air- Standard Assumptions; An Overview of Reciprocating Engines;
7)   Gas Power Cycles: Otto Cycle (The Ideal Cycle for Spark-Ignition Engine); Diesel Cycle (The Ideal Cycle for Compression-Ignition Engine);
8)   Gas Power Cycles: Stirling and Ericsson Cycles; Brayton Cycles (The Ideal Cycle for Gas-Turbine Engine); Ideal Jet-Propulsion Cycles; 2nd-law Analysis of Gas Power Cycles;
9)   期中考;
10)  Vapor and Combined Power Cycles: The Carnot Vapor Cycle; Energy Analysis of the Ideal Rankine Cycle;
11)  Vapor and Combined Power Cycles: Deviation of actual Vapor Power Cycles from Ideal Rankine Cycle; How to Increase Efficiency of the Rankine Cycle?
12)  Vapor and Combined Power Cycles: The Ideal Reheat Rankine Cycle;
13)  Vapor and Combined Power Cycles: The Ideal Regenerative Rankine Cycle;
14)  Vapor and Combined Power Cycles: 2nd-law Analysis of Vapor Power Cycles; Cogeneration;
15)  Chemical Reactions: Fuels and Combustions; Combustion Processes; Enthalpy of Formation and Enthalpy of Combustion;
16)  Chemical Reactions: First-law Analysis of Steady-Flow Reacting Systems; First-law Analysis of Closed Reacting Systems; Adiabatic Flame Temperature;
17)  Chemical Reactions: Entropy Change of Reacting Systems; 2nd-law Analysis of Reacting Systems;
18)  期末考
